{
  "coreName": "RPCS3",
  "systemId": "PS3",
  "extensions": {
    ".elf": "PS3",
    ".self": "PS3",
    ".bin": "PS3",
    ".iso": "PS3"
  },
  "author": "the RPCS3 Team",
  "url": "https://github.com/RPCS3/rpcs3",
  "romFile": "game",
  "deterministic": true,
  "memoryLayoutMiB": [
    512,
    16,
    64,
    256,
    20480
  ],
  "_memoryLayoutMiB_note": "sbrk, sealed, invisible, plain, mmap. The PS3's flat 4 GiB guest view (aligned to 4 GiB, so the arena spends 8 to place it), the 10 GiB execution table (8 GiB of dispatch pointers plus the segment map), rpcs3's 2 GiB JIT arena and every large allocation of the emulator all come out of the mmap arena; the block spans several 4 GiB regions, which is miniBox spec v2.",
  "video": {
    "_comment": "buffer CAPACITY: the PS3 outputs up to 1920x1080; the live size comes from GetVideoWidth/Height per frame and follows the display buffer the machine flips. 720p is the console's usual mode. 60 Hz exactly: the vblank thread schedules in whole microseconds of machine time.",
    "width": 1920,
    "height": 1080,
    "virtualWidth": 1280,
    "virtualHeight": 720,
    "vsyncNumerator": 60,
    "vsyncDenominator": 1,
    "getBgra": "GetVideoBgra"
  },
  "audio": {
    "_comment": "cellAudio's 48 kHz stereo mix, drained by machine time: 800 frames per vblank, silence when the machine mixed less.",
    "samplesPerFrame": 16384,
    "channels": 2,
    "get": "GetAudio"
  },
  "lag": {
    "inputWasRead": "InputWasRead"
  },
  "input": {
